WEBVTT

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:09.880
Pleased to meet you. I'm Yayoi Kunizuka.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.590
Good to see you again, Hinakawa.

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:14.720
Likewise.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:22.020
You're the legendary ex-enforcer who
reintegrated herself into society!

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:23.480
You're exaggerating.

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:27.190
You even got show business offers, right?

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:30.440
That's the legendary lady detective
for you.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:35.030
Today,

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:40.700
I'm here to report what I've learned about
abandoned zone transport businesses.

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:45.540
Draw the knives
locked behind your eyelids.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:49.340
Reap the lives that grow into shackles.

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:53.050
Even the lost memories that flee
once they're liberated and banished

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:56.010
Are an everlasting cubism.

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:16.910
Cause I know that in a future gone mad,

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:20.580
Even nightmares are peaceful.

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:22.700
RESET, RESET, yeah.

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:26.580
The midnight sun
awakens and turns to a riot.

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:31.210
A gun for a faux-friendly kiss.
A knife for a faux-revolutionary hug.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:37.430
Get rid of it all, even the frozen chains.

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:41.430
Reality is always outside your head.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:46.100
In a world seen through bestial eyes,

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:52.070
There is neither darkness nor light.

00:01:56.490 --> 00:01:59.780
Draw the knives
locked behind your eyelids.

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:03.450
Reap the lives that grow into shackles.

00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:07.120
Even the false memories that flash before
your eyes impatiently and impulsively

00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:09.790
Are an everlasting cubism.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:14.800
#04
Political Strife in the Colosseum

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:17.470
Abandoned zone transporters?

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:20.840
I thought the easiest way
to transport people

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:24.640
with deteriorated Hues
is to pass them off as dead.

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:30.190
In other words, culprits avoided street
scanners using suspended animation.

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:35.820
That'd be easily accomplished by using
drugs to induce and revive them.

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:40.160
Although they'd run
considerable physical risks.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:45.080
Hang on. Wouldn't that cloud
the transporters' Hues, too?

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:47.290
Which means...

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:51.170
Right. The transporters knew nothing
about their cargo.

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:55.840
I checked transport records
on the day of the attack.

00:02:56.460 --> 00:03:00.010
There was a complicated relay
between transport companies,

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:05.850
but I found one company that didn't follow
their scheduled shipping route.

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:11.600
Amimoto Transportation

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:13.230
Myogadani.

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:17.360
We've got you now, Enomiya.

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:19.190
Hey!

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:22.530
I've got a major lead, too.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:28.250
According to my intel,
Dr. Tsuchiya kept an office

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:31.040
in the Akihabara Abandoned Zone.

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:33.330
I'm amazed you found it.

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:35.920
I'm just good at giving orders.

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:37.380
Meaning?

00:03:37.710 --> 00:03:39.670
I told the informant

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:45.890
to check obscure places
like the borders of the abandoned zones.

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:48.010
That's not all, right?

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:50.770
He wouldn't rent it in his own name,

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:54.650
so I guessed he'd use
a friend or relative's.

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:58.150
He was using his late daughter's.

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:00.150
I see.

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:05.160
But should we really be following up
on Irie's lead first?

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:07.580
What's that supposed to mean?

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:09.290
Now, now.

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:12.330
Let's start by investigating Dr. Tsuchiya.

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:16.460
Are you trying to get
the big picture of the case?

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:17.750
I am.

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:23.300
By the way, how long
will Inspector Ignatov's suspension last?

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:25.930
Are you worried about him?

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:27.430
Of course not!

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:57.790
This is something else.

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:05.300
What's that?

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:07.340
A home secretary?

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:11.720
I am an assistant AI,
designation Prototype Ai.

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:15.560
You are hereby charged with trespassing.

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:20.520
Vacate the premises immediately,
or you will be reported to Public Safety.

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:24.150
We are Public Safety.

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:33.160
Identification complete.

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:37.210
I have a question.

00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:40.960
Has something happened to Dr. Tsuchiya?

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:46.220
You don't know?
You must be an offline AI, then.

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:48.890
The doctor is dead.

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:51.220
Probably murdered.

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:55.310
This eventuality was predicted
by the doctor.

00:05:55.890 --> 00:06:00.560
In the event of a suspected homicide,
I am to dispose of projects in progress.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:04.480
Switching to priority target
protection and aid protocol.

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:08.860
Which means?

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:12.120
I will cooperate
with the Public Safety Bureau.

00:06:12.910 --> 00:06:15.250
What is violence?

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:21.170
Is it not something that arises
when many people

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:24.420
seek something at the same time?

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:30.640
Everyone wants to lead a better life
with their heads held high.

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:35.770
That is why conflict and contempt
exist between us.

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:39.810
That is what I believe violence to be.

00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:45.570
Are you familiar with the term
"cognitive load"?

00:06:47.690 --> 00:06:49.900
Can you put it in layman's terms?

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:54.160
The human brain weighs
approximately three pounds.

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:57.450
About three percent
of the average body weight.

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:03.670
Nevertheless, it uses roughly 20 percent
of the energy expended in a day.

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:07.340
As a result,
the brain always desires to rest

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:12.760
and be free from worry.
That is cognitive load.

00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:17.220
Government is the only way

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:20.980
to minimize that violence
and bring happiness to you all.

00:07:22.190 --> 00:07:26.020
That's why I want to become a politician.

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:32.950
Dr. Tsuchiya wanted
to control this cognitive load externally.

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:37.950
To produce speech patterns and tones of
voice that would have the most influence

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:41.210
on the human decision-making process,

00:07:41.750 --> 00:07:44.880
he created
a new-generation artificial intelligence.

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:50.260
By equipping this mass-control AI
with a hologram generator

00:07:50.840 --> 00:07:55.970
capable of producing a perfect copy
of the outward appearance of a human,

00:07:56.510 --> 00:08:02.310
Dr. Tsuchiya created Mass-Control Karina,
also known as "Ma-Karina."

00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:06.360
Karina Komiya and Ma-Karina.

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:11.070
The doctor tried to protect
the AI he created.

00:08:11.650 --> 00:08:14.610
But Karina Komiya
probably took it from him.

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:20.080
So it was the AI the doctor was stalking,
not Karina?

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:25.500
Wait, hang on. We don't have evidence
of murder. Who are you saying did it?

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:30.050
Someone who wanted Karina Komiya
to win the election.

00:08:31.050 --> 00:08:37.010
They wanted to stop the doctor acting out,
and to keep Ma-Karina a secret.

00:08:44.980 --> 00:08:47.770
Thank you, Ma-Karina.

00:08:48.770 --> 00:08:50.860
Thank you, Karina.

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:54.490
Together, we can do anything.

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:57.410
We're not even a millisecond off.

00:08:58.370 --> 00:09:00.330
We're perfect.

00:09:05.210 --> 00:09:07.210
We're not even a millisecond off.

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:09.880
We're perfect.

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:15.220
Inspector, a transport company
linked to Enomiya is active.

00:09:15.880 --> 00:09:16.840
Don't tell me...

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:19.300
There's a debate today.

00:09:19.760 --> 00:09:21.600
Are they en route to Giga Arena?

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:23.430
That's right.

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:26.440
How's security at the arena?

00:09:28.350 --> 00:09:33.860
Bando and Seo from Unit Two are
on the scene. Drones have been deployed.

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:36.910
They must have drone countermeasures.

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:38.070
Kei?!

00:09:38.530 --> 00:09:40.660
I just arrived at Giga Arena.

00:09:40.950 --> 00:09:44.000
What? Aren't you suspended?

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:47.620
I simply came to hear the debate.

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:53.300
If I happen to see something suspicious,
I'll call... I mean, report it.

00:09:53.800 --> 00:09:54.550
Goodbye.

00:09:55.970 --> 00:09:58.180
He's pushing his luck.

00:09:58.300 --> 00:10:00.140
Hey, is he going to be OK?

00:10:00.760 --> 00:10:05.850
In any case, Enomiya plans
to attack the debate. Let's hurry.

00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:12.480
Komiya is betting everything
on this debate. We can't cancel it!

00:10:12.730 --> 00:10:15.280
Don't you care about her safety?

00:10:18.450 --> 00:10:20.280
Hello. This is Komiya.

00:10:20.740 --> 00:10:23.280
I'm Shindo from Public Safety.
We've met before.

00:10:24.330 --> 00:10:25.870
I've been filled in already.

00:10:26.870 --> 00:10:29.000
Am I at risk of being attacked?

00:10:29.420 --> 00:10:31.960
A dangerous person
named Enomiya is after you.

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:34.500
I see.

00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:37.010
I know your trick.

00:10:37.880 --> 00:10:39.180
I know about Ma-Karina.

00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:44.510
Enomiya will do anything it takes
to expose you.

00:10:46.520 --> 00:10:50.270
I can't afford to lose, Detective.

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:53.020
I'm not quitting.

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:54.730
Candidate Komiya!

00:10:56.860 --> 00:10:59.030
She's a tough nut to crack.

00:11:23.720 --> 00:11:24.640
It's time.

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:32.900
You're coming, Ms. Kunizuka?

00:11:33.650 --> 00:11:35.440
I'm in too deep to back out.

00:11:39.860 --> 00:11:43.070
The polls are currently tipping
in Komiya's favor.

00:11:44.660 --> 00:11:48.830
An idol lip-syncing to a full-body holo
is coming back from behind.

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:51.370
The Yakushiji campaign must be furious.

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:55.380
Aren't there restrictions
on civilian full-body holograms?

00:11:56.000 --> 00:12:00.050
That's why she's hiding it.
Even I was fooled.

00:12:00.420 --> 00:12:02.260
I don't really get it.

00:12:02.590 --> 00:12:06.510
What's it come down to?
An AI speechwriter, right?

00:12:07.260 --> 00:12:09.100
It's a lot more than that.

00:12:10.390 --> 00:12:11.430
It's neuroscience.

00:12:11.810 --> 00:12:17.480
A new mental control system applying
decision-making and cognitive psychology.

00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:22.900
An AI controlling humans?
Is that even possible?

00:12:23.780 --> 00:12:25.490
As a matter of fact,

00:12:25.780 --> 00:12:30.080
humans aren't very good at thinking
for themselves and making decisions.

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:34.790
It's a system that encourages people
to abandon thinking?

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:38.090
But humans will think anyway, won't they?

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:42.590
I know just what you're saying, Inspector.

00:12:43.220 --> 00:12:45.510
The more I learn about journalism,

00:12:45.890 --> 00:12:49.720
the more I realize how easy it is
for people to accept information

00:12:50.140 --> 00:12:52.600
without critical thought.

00:12:53.560 --> 00:12:57.270
Especially in our society,
where all our life choices

00:12:57.940 --> 00:12:59.940
are relegated to the authorities.

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:10.160
Inspector Bando, this is...

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:22.420
It's time for the final debate between
the top two frontrunners!

00:13:23.130 --> 00:13:25.590
Let's bring our candidates on stage!

00:13:25.840 --> 00:13:28.300
Candidate Kosuke Yakushiji!

00:13:35.350 --> 00:13:38.600
And Candidate Karina Komiya!

00:13:50.990 --> 00:13:52.950
Lock the cops up somewhere.

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:54.160
Got it.

00:13:58.370 --> 00:14:01.670
Limit the jamming area
so it doesn't stop the broadcast.

00:14:02.050 --> 00:14:02.840
Sure.

00:14:06.800 --> 00:14:11.760
So, who do you think did it?
Komiya or Yakushiji?

00:14:12.510 --> 00:14:16.180
Their Hues are both clear.
Could be someone else.

00:14:16.730 --> 00:14:17.520
That can't...

00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:19.350
That might be it.

00:14:20.270 --> 00:14:22.820
Both of them really don't know anything.

00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:26.190
Neither of them is involved in this case.

00:14:26.490 --> 00:14:27.530
What?

00:14:28.070 --> 00:14:32.780
But someone has to have planned this
and ordered its execution.

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:39.040
Someone who wants to control the entire
election through the frontrunners.

00:14:40.750 --> 00:14:43.380
Someone with ties to Enomiya.

00:15:24.460 --> 00:15:25.250
What was that?

00:15:26.550 --> 00:15:29.380
We seem to be having
some technical difficulties.

00:15:29.510 --> 00:15:31.760
Please remain calm.

00:15:35.680 --> 00:15:37.680
Who are you?

00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:49.240
Who do you think you are?

00:15:52.070 --> 00:15:53.820
Hey there, "champion"!

00:15:54.490 --> 00:15:55.160
Sir!

00:16:04.710 --> 00:16:07.590
No! Stop! Let go of me!

00:16:07.710 --> 00:16:08.800
Ma-Karina!

00:16:09.840 --> 00:16:11.800
Karina.

00:16:24.730 --> 00:16:26.560
Error. Reinitializing.

00:16:27.190 --> 00:16:28.610
Initialization failed.

00:16:29.480 --> 00:16:31.320
Campaign speech.

00:16:32.030 --> 00:16:35.660
Public debate simulation. Synchronizing.

00:16:36.410 --> 00:16:37.660
Synchronization failed.

00:16:41.370 --> 00:16:44.120
What... is... violence?

00:16:44.460 --> 00:16:48.670
Is it not some...thing that arises
when... many people...

00:16:49.420 --> 00:16:52.260
seek... something at... the same... time?

00:16:52.760 --> 00:16:55.180
Something... that...

00:17:00.560 --> 00:17:02.850
Is Karina a holo?

00:17:10.440 --> 00:17:13.030
Hinakawa, Kisaragi, direct the spectators.

00:17:13.280 --> 00:17:14.110
Yes, sir.

00:17:14.280 --> 00:17:17.740
Use call signs in any wireless
communication from now on.

00:17:18.530 --> 00:17:19.450
Stay alert.

00:17:32.050 --> 00:17:33.130
Apologize.

00:17:34.090 --> 00:17:37.010
We exposed your trick
before the public eye.

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:40.560
Apologize for deceiving the people.

00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:43.680
Do what we say, and we'll spare your life.

00:17:45.270 --> 00:17:46.520
I refuse.

00:17:47.440 --> 00:17:48.310
Karina!

00:17:49.860 --> 00:17:50.570
Stay away!

00:18:19.390 --> 00:18:20.220
Run!

00:18:21.470 --> 00:18:22.220
Get her!

00:18:34.570 --> 00:18:38.780
Please, no pushing. Remain calm.

00:18:42.410 --> 00:18:44.540
The broadcast's still running.

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:51.630
There!

00:18:53.710 --> 00:18:54.420
Damn.

00:18:59.630 --> 00:19:00.300
After her!

00:19:01.260 --> 00:19:03.640
Crime Coefficient is 335.

00:19:04.140 --> 00:19:05.850
Lethal Eliminator.

00:19:06.220 --> 00:19:08.100
Eliminate the target.

00:19:17.860 --> 00:19:20.030
Retake control of the security room.

00:19:20.530 --> 00:19:23.070
We need it to stop the broadcast
and direct people.

00:19:23.820 --> 00:19:24.990
I'll go.

00:19:26.200 --> 00:19:28.830
Hound 2, go with Kunizuka.

00:19:29.540 --> 00:19:32.000
Hound 3 and I
will pursue Candidate Komiya.

00:19:32.210 --> 00:19:33.000
Roger.

00:20:44.950 --> 00:20:45.780
I'm in, Shion.

00:20:46.820 --> 00:20:47.780
Hi there.

00:20:49.240 --> 00:20:50.040
Who's she?

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:53.250
Help the chief brought in.

00:20:55.670 --> 00:20:57.170
Can we leave this to you?

00:20:57.460 --> 00:20:58.790
I'm used to it.

00:21:00.460 --> 00:21:03.630
Good grief.
You're supposed to be suspended.

00:21:05.050 --> 00:21:07.010
I just got caught up in this.

00:21:07.970 --> 00:21:09.600
So I have no Dominator.

00:21:10.010 --> 00:21:11.140
I don't mean that.

00:21:11.520 --> 00:21:17.690
Inspectors are all about taking orders and
getting ahead. Should you be doing this?

00:21:18.610 --> 00:21:22.360
That doesn't matter.
What I do is up to me.

00:21:24.450 --> 00:21:25.450
Here you go.

00:21:25.610 --> 00:21:27.950
I got their position. I'll send it now.

00:21:28.160 --> 00:21:28.780
Please do.

00:21:32.830 --> 00:21:33.450
Hey,

00:21:34.750 --> 00:21:38.380
did Sibyl partner you
with Inspector Shindo?

00:21:38.960 --> 00:21:42.300
No. Our compatibility results
didn't recommend it.

00:21:42.670 --> 00:21:45.050
Just the opposite, in fact.

00:21:45.840 --> 00:21:48.510
So, you're ignoring Sibyl's determination?

00:21:49.140 --> 00:21:50.970
I trust Sibyl, of course,

00:21:51.600 --> 00:21:54.350
but the system isn't everything.

00:21:55.310 --> 00:21:57.310
That's what Arata and I believe.

00:21:59.020 --> 00:21:59.810
Here.

00:22:04.360 --> 00:22:05.690
You should at least have this.

00:22:06.570 --> 00:22:07.320
Thank you.

00:22:11.780 --> 00:22:13.830
Security camera image recognition set.

00:22:14.660 --> 00:22:18.000
We've found Karina Komiya.
I'll show you the route.

00:22:18.330 --> 00:22:19.000
Thank you.

00:22:30.220 --> 00:22:30.890
There she is!

00:22:40.270 --> 00:22:41.190
You're kidding!

00:22:49.910 --> 00:22:50.780
Oishi!

00:22:52.780 --> 00:22:54.370
Keep going, Shepherd 2!

00:22:54.620 --> 00:22:55.660
Thank you!

00:23:05.170 --> 00:23:10.720
Since you started sharing the abandoned
zone's information network with Tsunemori,

00:23:11.260 --> 00:23:15.720
something hasn't been right.
Don't you agree, Irie?

00:23:16.890 --> 00:23:18.850
What does it matter now?

00:23:19.140 --> 00:23:23.060
More importantly, Oishi,
is this what you wanted to do?

00:23:23.900 --> 00:23:25.320
Don't act like my boss.

00:23:25.900 --> 00:23:27.070
I'm not.

00:23:30.860 --> 00:23:32.450
Feel free to come at me.

00:23:42.040 --> 00:23:45.000
Stop! Let go of me!

00:24:27.840 --> 00:24:29.130
Orders updated.

00:24:29.510 --> 00:24:31.760
Permission to murder
Karina Komiya granted.

00:24:33.090 --> 00:24:35.840
Hey, Karina, do you trust me?

00:24:36.390 --> 00:24:39.430
What? Of course I don't.

00:24:39.560 --> 00:24:40.970
That's what I thought.

00:24:49.940 --> 00:24:51.900
Ow!

00:24:53.280 --> 00:24:54.490
Unbelievable.

00:24:57.370 --> 00:24:58.580
Hey there!

00:25:00.910 --> 00:25:01.620
Damn.

00:25:01.750 --> 00:25:02.790
I can't get a lock.

00:25:19.930 --> 00:25:22.100
What are you, a combat robot?

00:25:22.350 --> 00:25:25.520
He was Enomiya's bodyguard.

00:25:26.400 --> 00:25:27.560
Be careful.

00:25:27.860 --> 00:25:28.520
I will.

00:26:15.070 --> 00:26:16.610
Good grief.

00:26:18.110 --> 00:26:20.820
Beats an Eliminator blast, right?

00:26:47.730 --> 00:26:48.600
Let's do it!

00:26:48.980 --> 00:26:49.810
Right!

00:27:10.420 --> 00:27:11.540
Are you all right?

00:27:11.880 --> 00:27:14.460
Totally fine.

00:27:15.250 --> 00:27:15.840
Karina!

00:27:15.960 --> 00:27:16.590
En!

00:27:18.550 --> 00:27:21.470
All assailants secured or disposed of.

00:27:21.720 --> 00:27:22.970
Security drones back up.

00:27:23.600 --> 00:27:25.310
Unit Two's backup has arrived.

00:27:25.600 --> 00:27:26.970
Roger.

00:27:27.680 --> 00:27:31.140
They will take over
guarding Candidate Komiya.

00:27:33.610 --> 00:27:35.190
Thank you...

00:27:37.030 --> 00:27:38.490
Inspector Shindo!

00:27:45.410 --> 00:27:47.620
Please leave in an orderly fashion!

00:27:50.330 --> 00:27:51.620
Please come with us.

00:27:54.710 --> 00:27:56.380
What is the meaning of this?!

00:27:57.090 --> 00:27:59.510
Mr. Yakushiji was assaulted!

00:27:59.800 --> 00:28:02.260
A person named Enomiya planned the attack.

00:28:05.510 --> 00:28:06.390
What?

00:28:07.010 --> 00:28:10.020
If you keep wasting our time,
I'll enforce you!

00:28:10.350 --> 00:28:12.730
Who's enforcing who, you latent criminal?!

00:28:14.560 --> 00:28:16.230
Don't tell me about enforcement

00:28:16.400 --> 00:28:20.690
when you couldn't protect your parent
or your candidate!

00:28:22.150 --> 00:28:25.450
What? What are you talking about?

00:28:26.200 --> 00:28:28.580
That's enough. Stop.

00:28:34.000 --> 00:28:35.670
I won't run or hide.

00:28:36.080 --> 00:28:39.090
I want you to explain
exactly what's going on.

00:28:39.590 --> 00:28:41.210
I'd be delighted to.

00:28:41.760 --> 00:28:47.640
Please back up your slogan that
"a healthy mind dwells in a healthy body."

00:28:53.190 --> 00:28:54.020
Hey.

00:28:55.600 --> 00:28:58.150
I wish you a long and happy life.

00:29:03.110 --> 00:29:06.160
This is that mark, isn't it?

00:29:07.320 --> 00:29:09.700
I'll hold onto this.

00:29:11.330 --> 00:29:13.210
Hey, Temma.

00:29:13.710 --> 00:29:16.000
I won't make trouble for you.

00:29:30.720 --> 00:29:32.640
Good day, Second Inspector.

00:29:35.850 --> 00:29:37.190
You bastard.

00:29:37.600 --> 00:29:40.360
A word of warning, Enomiya.

00:29:40.820 --> 00:29:45.740
Make the right choices from now on,
and you'll survive.

00:29:46.320 --> 00:29:47.360
Cut the crap!

00:29:48.530 --> 00:29:50.870
Oh my, don't tell me...

00:29:55.250 --> 00:29:57.830
You're thinking of doing something to...

00:30:00.630 --> 00:30:01.550
Ow!

00:30:02.170 --> 00:30:04.010
You're pretty fast.

00:30:04.670 --> 00:30:06.340
That's an ex-pro for you.

00:30:07.220 --> 00:30:07.840
Shut up!

00:30:14.180 --> 00:30:16.350
You're making the wrong choice.

00:30:42.420 --> 00:30:45.550
And you continue
to make the wrong choices.

00:31:17.410 --> 00:31:22.670
Karina Komiya's victory
was determined by Bifrost in advance.

00:31:24.800 --> 00:31:28.760
Your interference ended up
wringing Yakushiji's neck.

00:31:28.920 --> 00:31:30.840
That was the plan all along.

00:31:31.380 --> 00:31:35.600
You thought you were working
for Yakushiji, but you helped Komiya.

00:31:36.720 --> 00:31:39.850
Such a sad little puppet.
You bring a tear to my eye.

00:31:40.640 --> 00:31:42.270
Did you set this up?!

00:31:42.520 --> 00:31:47.940
Oh no, I just noticed it.
It was the congressmen who arranged it.

00:31:48.320 --> 00:31:53.030
I'm sure they didn't just need Karina
Komiya to win. They cared how she won.

00:31:54.410 --> 00:31:57.540
You mean they used me as a card?!

00:31:58.080 --> 00:31:59.700
A sacrificial card.

00:32:00.870 --> 00:32:03.580
Oh, and you'd be safe
if you took the stairs.

00:32:04.130 --> 00:32:06.460
Lament your own stupidity.

00:32:07.550 --> 00:32:10.090
Azusawa!

00:32:17.260 --> 00:32:18.890
Goodbye, Enomiya.

00:32:19.310 --> 00:32:23.100
You weren't pretty and you weren't nice.

00:32:27.020 --> 00:32:29.480
Do you know why I called you here?

00:32:29.860 --> 00:32:33.490
For interfering in a case while suspended.
I have no excuse.

00:32:33.780 --> 00:32:36.280
Inspector Ignatov isn't to blame.

00:32:36.620 --> 00:32:38.240
As the inspector on site, I...

00:32:38.370 --> 00:32:41.120
Suspension? What suspension?

00:32:41.450 --> 00:32:42.500
Huh?

00:32:42.960 --> 00:32:46.000
Less than an hour
before the incident at the debate,

00:32:46.630 --> 00:32:50.170
the bureau chief and I
lifted Inspector Ignatov's suspension

00:32:50.340 --> 00:32:53.550
as a special anti-terrorism measure.

00:32:54.680 --> 00:32:57.350
Listen, that was a close call.

00:32:58.010 --> 00:33:00.270
You won't get any second chances.

00:33:01.220 --> 00:33:02.020
Yes, ma'am!

00:33:03.140 --> 00:33:06.270
Thank goodness Chief Shimotsuki
is a scheming fox.

00:33:06.560 --> 00:33:09.110
Never say that to her face.

00:33:10.360 --> 00:33:12.280
Candidate Karina Komiya...

00:33:12.570 --> 00:33:15.570
Non-alcoholic for you, Yayoi.

00:33:16.030 --> 00:33:17.660
Don't worry about me so much.

00:33:18.450 --> 00:33:23.540
You worked hard to return to society.
We can't have alcohol clouding your Hue.

00:33:23.870 --> 00:33:26.710
The turbulent gubernatorial election
is nearly over.

00:33:27.080 --> 00:33:29.710
The results will be announced momentarily.

00:33:30.420 --> 00:33:31.920
Did you vote?

00:33:32.340 --> 00:33:35.090
I did, but I won't say who for.

00:33:35.430 --> 00:33:37.720
Come on, you can tell me.

00:33:37.840 --> 00:33:39.800
Whoa, you reek of alcohol!

00:33:40.180 --> 00:33:43.520
Enforcers don't have voting rights.

00:33:44.060 --> 00:33:47.520
I'm so jealous you get to!

00:33:48.230 --> 00:33:50.570
So come on, tell me!

00:33:53.030 --> 00:33:56.570
The results are in.
The winner is Candidate Karina Komiya.

00:33:58.030 --> 00:33:59.240
Komiya, huh?

00:33:59.950 --> 00:34:02.700
So, Yakushiji fell short
of the gold medal.

00:34:03.750 --> 00:34:07.750
Candidate Karina Komiya already has
a five-percent lead in votes.

00:34:08.630 --> 00:34:13.630
Factoring in Hue correction, victory for
Candidate Yakushiji is now impossible.

00:34:14.340 --> 00:34:17.430
Candidate Yakushiji
has been stripped of Hue privilege.

00:34:17.970 --> 00:34:20.890
He'll be temporarily held
at the Public Safety Bureau.

00:34:21.010 --> 00:34:24.100
What? They're sending him here?

00:34:24.520 --> 00:34:27.480
He has a lot of social influence,
after all.

00:34:27.810 --> 00:34:30.610
He'll receive isolated counseling
and intensive care.

00:34:30.730 --> 00:34:33.690
If his Crime Coefficient
stays high after that...

00:34:35.650 --> 00:34:37.400
He'll be institutionalized.

00:34:37.900 --> 00:34:39.860
So long, Heracles.

00:34:40.530 --> 00:34:42.490
The gap is bigger than predicted.

00:34:42.990 --> 00:34:46.790
I guess the people gave tacit approval
to her use of AI.

00:34:47.160 --> 00:34:53.130
Ma-Karina getting exposed didn't matter.
People really don't sweat the small stuff.

00:34:54.170 --> 00:34:56.970
I wonder what constitutes an ideal human.

00:34:57.630 --> 00:34:59.340
What brought that on?

00:35:00.510 --> 00:35:02.140
How should I put it...?

00:35:02.850 --> 00:35:05.640
Yakushiji was doped up
to be the ideal athlete.

00:35:06.180 --> 00:35:09.520
Karina Komiya wanted to win at any cost.

00:35:11.190 --> 00:35:15.110
In the end, maybe the one
most in line with Sibyl

00:35:15.980 --> 00:35:17.650
was Ma-Karina, the AI.

00:35:18.030 --> 00:35:22.490
Relegate yourself to an external entity,
and your body becomes the avatar.

00:35:23.450 --> 00:35:27.000
That way of thinking
might find favor these days.

00:35:28.000 --> 00:35:28.830
Even so...

00:35:29.210 --> 00:35:31.370
The system isn't everything.

00:35:33.670 --> 00:35:35.050
I'm overjoyed.

00:35:35.420 --> 00:35:38.380
Thank you to all my supporters.

00:35:38.880 --> 00:35:42.930
I'm going to make politics fun,
like a concert or a TV show.

00:35:52.850 --> 00:35:54.020
What's up?

00:35:55.230 --> 00:35:56.860
Don't startle me!

00:35:57.230 --> 00:36:00.820
You came for the welcome party, right?
Come on in.

00:36:01.780 --> 00:36:07.200
But won't I be a wet blanket?

00:36:07.580 --> 00:36:09.330
It'll be fine.

00:36:09.450 --> 00:36:13.540
We're not that nervous around you, Chief.

00:36:13.750 --> 00:36:16.210
So you are nervous around me, then.

00:36:18.760 --> 00:36:24.720
Forget nervous. Without you, I'd be
rotting in an abandoned zone by now.

00:36:25.430 --> 00:36:26.510
That was...

00:36:28.640 --> 00:36:32.810
I just took over an information network.
It was...

00:36:34.770 --> 00:36:36.060
Akane's work.

00:36:38.440 --> 00:36:43.410
Merely leading Karina Komiya to victory
is not the true intent of Roundrobin.

00:36:43.700 --> 00:36:48.740
The issue was making the public
aware of her proxy personality AI

00:36:48.870 --> 00:36:52.000
and creating a situation
that Sibyl could not ignore.

00:36:52.410 --> 00:36:55.880
It was essential to our security.

00:36:56.000 --> 00:37:00.420
Although Kyoko curbing Enomiya
early on was rather unfortunate.

00:37:00.800 --> 00:37:03.930
I'm shocked you lost
all your past winnings.

00:37:04.130 --> 00:37:06.930
You could drop low enough
to face enforcement.

00:37:07.640 --> 00:37:10.720
I'd hate to see you go out like this,
Shizuka.

00:37:24.610 --> 00:37:27.240
Summoning off-duty inspectors now?

00:37:28.070 --> 00:37:29.660
You've come up in the world.

00:37:33.160 --> 00:37:34.410
Well, I am the governor.

00:37:36.620 --> 00:37:40.130
The doctor was stalking Ma-Karina,
not you.

00:37:40.340 --> 00:37:41.920
That was a red herring.

00:37:43.720 --> 00:37:47.590
Do you think children
are their parents' property, Detective?

00:37:48.180 --> 00:37:53.220
Children are believed to have independent
personalities since the modern era.

00:37:54.350 --> 00:37:55.770
What about AIs?

00:37:58.020 --> 00:38:02.480
Dr. Tsuchiya doted on Ma-Karina
as a substitute for his daughter.

00:38:03.490 --> 00:38:05.280
His late daughter?

00:38:05.700 --> 00:38:07.950
His murdered daughter, to be precise.

00:38:21.710 --> 00:38:25.720
It happened seven years ago,
during the Helmet Riots.

00:38:26.300 --> 00:38:29.680
You know, when people in weird helmets
caused a riot?

00:38:30.220 --> 00:38:30.970
Yes.

00:38:31.720 --> 00:38:36.310
The doctor pursued his research
in hopes that would never happen again.

00:38:36.680 --> 00:38:41.480
An Affirmation Party legislator supported
his work. That's how I came to use it.

00:38:42.690 --> 00:38:43.900
I see.

00:38:44.440 --> 00:38:48.490
The doctor's research was also
to make tools to heal himself.

00:38:49.280 --> 00:38:49.990
Yes.

00:38:51.030 --> 00:38:53.580
You and Ma-Karina are accomplices.

00:38:55.540 --> 00:38:59.000
Ma-Karina probably disliked
being used as a surrogate.

00:39:00.380 --> 00:39:02.500
She was advanced enough for that.

00:39:03.210 --> 00:39:04.750
Accomplices, huh?

00:39:06.510 --> 00:39:07.840
How official of you.

00:39:17.390 --> 00:39:18.640
But I'm glad.

00:39:20.560 --> 00:39:24.110
Neither you nor Ma-Karina wished
for the doctor's death.

00:39:25.070 --> 00:39:27.280
You wanted him to be healed.

00:39:30.410 --> 00:39:31.780
I saw you on TV.

00:39:32.820 --> 00:39:35.540
"Make politics fun, like a TV show."

00:39:36.580 --> 00:39:39.210
Those were Ma-Karina's words, by the way.

00:39:39.960 --> 00:39:44.670
TV shows come in all genres.
Just steer clear of thrillers or horror.

00:39:45.130 --> 00:39:47.260
Politics needs thrills, too.

00:39:48.510 --> 00:39:50.930
The Roman poet Juvenalis

00:39:51.180 --> 00:39:56.010
satirised the rulers of his time,
saying that they blinded the citizens

00:39:56.470 --> 00:39:58.470
with bread and circuses.

00:39:59.930 --> 00:40:02.850
What's wrong with that?
As long as there's peace.

00:40:03.440 --> 00:40:06.770
It's not like everyone
wants to keep their eyes open.

00:40:10.530 --> 00:40:14.410
Do you think I'm a good person,
or an evil one?

00:40:15.780 --> 00:40:17.660
What do you think yourself?

00:40:19.200 --> 00:40:20.410
An evil one, I guess.

00:40:22.420 --> 00:40:25.590
A lot of people have been ruined
because of me.

00:40:27.090 --> 00:40:29.760
You just refused to lose.

00:40:30.970 --> 00:40:33.930
I kind of like people
who call themselves evil.

00:40:36.510 --> 00:40:38.600
I'm glad I voted for you.

00:40:43.730 --> 00:40:49.280
So, why did you really call me out here?

00:40:50.740 --> 00:40:52.950
What will happen to Ma-Karina now?

00:40:53.860 --> 00:40:55.660
What's Sibyl's response?

00:40:56.450 --> 00:40:59.080
Sibyl recognized you as governor.

00:41:00.330 --> 00:41:03.830
Isn't that an answer enough?

00:41:09.460 --> 00:41:10.340
I suppose.

00:41:14.630 --> 00:41:16.140
Let's meet again soon.

00:41:17.100 --> 00:41:18.550
Don't catch a cold.

00:41:20.520 --> 00:41:22.430
Thanks for your concern.

00:41:39.530 --> 00:41:41.490
Haruki Enomiya died in an accident.

00:41:41.910 --> 00:41:47.380
By the time Unit Three arrived,
their underground casino was empty.

00:41:47.790 --> 00:41:50.500
Enomiya's body was the only thing left.

00:41:59.050 --> 00:42:00.010
Inspectors.

00:42:00.890 --> 00:42:03.220
What's wrong? You look serious.

00:42:04.390 --> 00:42:06.140
I have something for you.

00:42:11.360 --> 00:42:14.150
Enomiya's card
was among Yakushiji's effects.

00:42:15.070 --> 00:42:18.700
I got the other one when Irie,
the previous inspectors, and I

00:42:18.870 --> 00:42:22.410
spoke to this man
during an investigation.

00:42:28.370 --> 00:42:29.920
An investigation? Of what?

00:42:30.500 --> 00:42:35.800
Neither inspector told us what it was
we were investigating.

00:42:36.380 --> 00:42:38.680
Then there was an accident.

00:42:39.640 --> 00:42:43.640
One inspector died
and the other was institutionalized.

00:42:44.520 --> 00:42:46.980
Yes, I heard about that.

00:42:47.890 --> 00:42:51.690
The institutionalized one insists

00:42:51.810 --> 00:42:56.030
that it wasn't an accident. It was murder.

00:42:57.450 --> 00:42:59.490
Says a fox bit them.

00:43:22.050 --> 00:43:22.930
No.

00:43:24.180 --> 00:43:25.680
I don't want to, Dad.

00:43:35.860 --> 00:43:38.610
You're closing the investigation
on the Enomiya case?

00:43:39.700 --> 00:43:41.860
We won't find anything more.

00:43:42.700 --> 00:43:48.450
As with Unit One's former inspectors,
it both was, and was not, an accident.

00:43:50.330 --> 00:43:52.630
"Bitten by a fox," was it?

00:43:53.710 --> 00:43:59.010
Is this a challenge to the system,
or an inadmissible bug in it?

00:44:01.050 --> 00:44:04.890
Either way, make good use of those two.

00:44:05.850 --> 00:44:10.310
I know. I will flush out the foxes.

00:44:11.390 --> 00:44:13.650
At any cost.

00:44:28.660 --> 00:44:31.750
Stupid perfection in your own castle

00:44:33.920 --> 00:44:37.590
How smart. You cause me to yawn

00:44:38.880 --> 00:44:44.430
Look,
The key to the door is in your hand

00:44:44.550 --> 00:44:49.640
Don't you let anyone take control

00:44:49.770 --> 00:44:54.980
What do you want?

00:44:55.100 --> 00:45:00.280
Go get it. Play by your own rule

00:45:00.400 --> 00:45:06.200
The winner always controls the game

00:45:06.320 --> 00:45:11.200
You stand in your belief

00:45:14.580 --> 00:45:19.130
There's no promising future

00:45:19.500 --> 00:45:24.630
Always helpless
Crying for the moon

00:45:24.760 --> 00:45:29.970
Finger trembles in fear
With the weight of the trigger

00:45:30.140 --> 00:45:33.180
There's a way for us

00:45:33.310 --> 00:45:37.230
Show them how we fight

00:45:37.360 --> 00:45:40.480
Pull the trigger

00:45:45.570 --> 00:45:47.740
"Psycho-Pass" refers to the measurement
of a person's mind and personality.

00:45:47.870 --> 00:45:49.870
This is a work of fiction. Any resemblance
to real persons or groups is coincidental.
